# Ship commands — UCPH vs CMPH vs SWAT

The user runs the product, not the docs. When the change is runnable, do not spend the turn on plan, status, or handoff prose before they have something to run.

Close-out words name the **work**. Green tests are not permission.

| Command | Permission to | What the agent does |
|---------|---------------|---------------------|
| **UCPH** | Park WIP on the **feature branch** (no `main`) | After the human check **PASS** (or an explicit waive): confirm evidence, harvest if needed, merge-ready gate, truth docs, **commit**, **`git push -u origin <feature-branch>`**, Receiver brief. Does **not** merge, delete the branch, or run reviewer skills. |
| **CMPH** | Land this ship on `main` | Same truth, docs, and tests as UCPH, then **merge to `main`** and **push `origin main`**. **Keep** the feature branch. Does **not** run reviewer skills. |
| **CMPHD** | Land on `main` and **delete** the feature branch | Same as CMPH, then delete local and remote. Only this command (or an explicit “delete the branch”) may delete. |
| **SWAT** | Close the epic | code-reviewer; dead-code-remover when that skill is available; tech-debt-evaluator; security-reviewer only if the epic touched credentials, logging, networking, or files; merge-ready gate; then [epic-close.mdc](epic-close.mdc). Does **not** merge a mid-epic story by itself. |

**UCPH** = update docs, commit, push the feature branch, handoff. Synonyms: “park the branch”, “docs commit push handoff”. **Not** merge permission.

Every UCPH and CMPH Receiver brief includes this line verbatim, between **Next steps** and **Measured**: `write thorough tests. red, integration, find missing ones of both kinds.`

**WRAP** / “land it” / “merge to main” / “ship to main” = **CMPH** (keep the branch). **CMPHD** = the same land, then delete. After they say it, do not ask “merge?” again.

**Do not merge** until both are true: the CMPH work above is done or running this turn, **and** they granted CMPH permission this conversation. See [no-auto-merge-main.mdc](no-auto-merge-main.mdc).

**Do not run SWAT** until both are true: that work is the job this turn, **and** they typed **SWAT**, or this CMPH is the epic’s last in-scope story (that CMPH includes SWAT). A mid-epic CMPH or UCPH is not SWAT permission.

## Fast loop (default)

1. Code plus red/green for the piece, and an integration test that runs it together with the shipped chain it belongs to ([integration-chain.mdc](integration-chain.mdc)).
2. The merge-ready command in AGENT_HANDOFF. If the stack compiles, count every documented compile ([testing.mdc](testing.mdc)).
3. If this ship is user-visible, bump the public version in the same change ([pm-versioning.mdc](pm-versioning.mdc)). Docs-only ships do not bump.
4. Run the documented install or run step.
5. Ask with the shape in [human-check.mdc](human-check.mdc).

Nothing else. No plan essay, no reviewer skills, no handoff note, until they say **UCPH**, **CMPH**, or **SWAT**.

## Still mandatory inside the fast loop

- Human **PASS** (or an explicit waive) before commit, when the ship changes what they run ([human-check.mdc](human-check.mdc)).
- A named Tier 1 test for any lock that can be expressed without the runtime ([testing.mdc](testing.mdc)).
- The integration chain for the behaviors this change sits in, not only the new unit test ([integration-chain.mdc](integration-chain.mdc)).
- Measured numbers in chat when a runtime session produced them. “See the log” is not a verdict.

## Forbidden

- Reviewer, dead-code, or tech-debt skills on a mid-epic **UCPH** or **CMPH**.
- Handoff or status prose in the same turn as a fix, unless they said **UCPH**, **CMPH**, or **SWAT**.
- Treating **UCPH** as permission to merge `main`.
- Using “the docs are not updated yet” to delay a build they can run.
